==German==

===Etymology===
Attested ca. 1500, standard since the 18th century. From an {{der|de|gmw-ecg|-}} dialect word, equivalent to {{suf|de|Schmetten|t1=cream|-ling}}, due to an old belief that butterflies eat milk products or, in a more ornamented form, that witches transform themselves into butterflies in order to steal such products.<ref>[https://www.dwds.de/wb/Schmetterling Schmetterling], in: W. Pfeifer et al., ''Etymologisches Wörterbuch des Deutschen'', 1993.</ref> Compare {{m+|en|butterfly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃmɛtərlɪŋ/|[ˈʃmɛtɐlɪŋ]}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schmetterling.ogg|audio (Germany)}}

